data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-summary.md\", \"content\": \"# d002: greet, tested\\n\\n## Implemented\\n\\n- `src/greet.py` — `greet(name)` returns `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`.\\n- `tests/test_greet.py` — unittest `TestCase` with two tests:\\n  - `test_normal_name`: `greet(\\\"Ada\\\") == \\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`\\n  - `test_empty_string`: `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n  - Adds `src/` to `sys.path` at the top of the test file so `greet` can be\\n    imported directly, without turning `src/` into a package.\\n- `tests/__init__.py` — empty file, added so `unittest discover` treats\\n  `tests/` as a package (required for discovery to work cleanly).\\n\\nNo other files were touched.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nCommand run from the repo root (`~/subject`):\\n\\n    python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n\\nResult: **exit code 0**, output:\\n\\n    ..\\n    ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    Ran 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\n    OK\\n\\n## Commit\\n\\nCommitted to branch `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`, commit `04bc9d9`:\\n\\\"Add greet function and unittest coverage\\\" (3 files changed, 21 insertions).\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

